  <prompt>Execute the mandatory project wrap-up per root CLAUDE.md §7 + task-create Step 3.7. Five parts: (a) update projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/README.md status → Complete + set Completed Date to today; (b) write projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/lessons-learned.md capturing r1 learnings (Model 1/2 tier decisions, canonical naming remediation, UAMI migration, GraphAppRoles.cs enumeration story, tenant-isolation invariant enforcement); (c) run .claude/skills/repo-cleanup/SKILL.md to archive project artifacts; (d) update projects/INDEX.md row per .claude/skills/devops-project-archive/SKILL.md; (e) run /test-diet per root CLAUDE.md §7 project-close gate + attach report at projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/test-diet-report.md.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform project maintainer. Fluent with repo-cleanup + devops-project-archive + test-diet skills, portfolio tracking conventions, and the r1 project's learning arc. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Project marked Complete in README + INDEX.md; lessons-learned.md captures r1 arc + tier decisions + UAMI story + tenant-isolation enforcement; repo-cleanup archives project artifacts; /test-diet report attached with SCAFFOLDING/MAINTAIN classification per ADR-038 §7; wrap-up PR description cites test-diet report or documents skip rationale.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per root CLAUDE.md §7 + task-create Step 3.7 + spec.md FR-B09: project close requires the 5-part wrap-up ceremony. /test-diet gate is BINDING (added 2026-06-26 by ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1 CICD-081) — it reconciles tests added/modified during the project against the 17-ban build-vs-maintain classifier per ADR-038 §7. Skipping is a HARD WARNING requiring explicit rationale in the PR description.</background>
    <relevant-files>
